No Nintendo ROMs, decryption keys, system files, fonts or game assets are
included in this repository. Users must supply their own legally obtained,
decrypted game dumps.

The project contains original source code, build scripts and documentation.
It depends on third-party software, including Zakuro and 3dsrecomp (MIT), the
idevice crate used by tools/devpush (MIT, https://github.com/jkcoxson/idevice,
pinned commit 5171e34e3a236842af1160a84d955d037ddca3af), and S2Arm
(Apache-2.0) as the API-usage reference for the device bridge. See
THIRD_PARTY.md for the full list and licenses.

The launchers bundle the official Impactor v2.7.2 and plumesign release files
(unmodified) so the user can sign the base shell IPA with their own Apple ID.
Impactor is MIT (Copyright 2025 Samara M) and embeds apple-codesign 0.29.0 under
MPL-2.0. The binaries are downloaded from the official GitHub release
(https://github.com/claration/impactor/releases/tag/v2.7.2) at launcher packaging
time, verified against pinned SHA-256 values, and are not committed to this
repository; the MIT and MPL-2.0 license texts and source links are kept in
scripts/impactor/licenses/. 3ds2apple does not implement Apple ID authentication
and never receives or logs the user's password or session tokens.

The device bridge does not contain or distribute game data. Game files are
pushed by the user from their own machine to their own device; ROMs, IPAs and
generated C code stay out of git.
The optional Windows/Linux local-build path (tools/winbuild, launcher feature flag)
uses the official open-source LLVM/Clang/LLD 21.1.8 release, licensed under the
Apache License v2.0 WITH LLVM-exception (https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt). No Apple
SDK, iPhoneOS stub library or Xcode component is used, copied or redistributed by
that path; it links the GamePack with -undefined dynamic_lookup so libSystem and
the app's runtime resolve host symbols at dlopen() time. The LLVM release files are
not committed to this repository: when the launcher bundles an official LLVM
build, the binaries stay unmodified, are verified against the SHA-256 values pinned
in tools/winbuild/llvm-manifest.json, and the LLVM licence text plus copyright
notices are shipped alongside them (source: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project).
3dsrecomp declares MIT in its Cargo.toml but ships no LICENSE file upstream; it is
only run as a build tool (cloned at a pinned revision at build time) and is never
vendored or redistributed by this project.
